        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 17.5.7. Nothing herein shall be construed to limit the Union's lawful rights to determine and enforce regulations regarding acquisition of, and retention of, membership in the Union. Any covered regular employee who is refused membership, or whose membership is involuntarily terminated by action of the Union body (other than for refusal to tender initiation fee and periodic dues) shall not be subject to discharge from employment but, rather, shall take on the status of a Service Fee Employee.",
